---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';

const title = 'Characters & Story | Mystery Emblem, a Pokémon Fire Emblem Fan Game';
const description =
  'Meet the cast of Mystery Emblem: your Dragon hero, Piplup, Flabébé, Wimpod, Sir Empoleon, and the Pokémon you can recruit across the Verdant Heartland.';
---

<InfoPageLayout title={title} description={description} heading="Characters & Story">
  <p>
    The continent was once kept safe by the Dragon Kingdom, until the royal tactician Gengar betrayed
    it and tore open a rift called the Abyss. Now the Abyss is spreading, wild Pokémon are turning
    Feral, and the Ironscale Empire is using the chaos to march across the land.
  </p>

  <h2>Your team</h2>

  <h3>You: the Dragon hero</h3>
  <p>
    A personality quiz decides which Dragon-type Pokémon you are: <strong>Axew</strong>,
    <strong>Bagon</strong>, <strong>Gible</strong>, <strong>Dratini</strong>, or <strong>Goomy</strong>.
    You grew up in a coastal village of the Verdant Commonwealth, raised as family by Sir Empoleon,
    with no idea where you really came from.
  </p>

  <h3>Piplup</h3>
  <p>
    Sir Empoleon's son and your best friend. Proud, loyal, and always first into a fight. He dreams of
    becoming a royal knight like his dad.
  </p>

  <h3>Flabébé</h3>
  <p>
    Your kind, level-headed childhood friend and the team's healer. Her flower color matches whichever
    Dragon you are.
  </p>

  <h3>Wimpod</h3>
  <p>
    A self-declared coward who would much rather hide behind a rock. He doesn't fight, but he's always
    the first to spot danger, and he's the one who explains new things as you play.
  </p>

  <h3>Sir Empoleon</h3>
  <p>
    A knight of the Royal Guard and your foster father. Strict on the training ground and fiercely
    protective everywhere else. He joins the fight as an experienced veteran.
  </p>

  <h2>Pokémon you can recruit</h2>
  <p>Along the way, new allies join your team. Some depend on your quiz answers:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Pidgey, Starly, or Pikipek</strong>, and <strong>Sewaddle</strong>: a bird and a bug who call a truce mid-chase.</li>
    <li><strong>Abra, Ralts, or Solosis</strong>: a frightened psychic lost in the mountains.</li>
    <li><strong>Elekid or Pawmi</strong>: an old friend from your village.</li>
    <li><strong>Slakoth</strong>: found napping in the middle of a raid (optional side chapter).</li>
    <li><strong>Duskull</strong>: the solemn caretaker of a mountain shrine.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Allies and rivals</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>King Serperior and Lady Milotic</strong> rule the Verdant Commonwealth with wisdom and grace.</li>
    <li><strong>Kecleon</strong>, a traveling merchant, opens shops across the map once you rescue him.</li>
    <li><strong>Commander Deino</strong> is a young Dragon like you, raised by the Ironscale Empire and loyal to it.</li>
    <li><strong>Emperor Kingambit</strong> leads the Ironscale Empire and claims that only his iron rule can stop the Abyss.</li>
    <li><strong>Gengar</strong>, the traitor, still schemes from the shadows.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The world</h2>
  <p>
    The demo takes place in the <strong>Verdant Heartland</strong>: beaches, mountain passes, river
    shrines, berry orchards, and a border fortress. Beyond it lie the desert kingdom of Goldensand and
    the lands of the Ironscale Empire. Read more <a href="/about/">about the game</a>, or learn
    <a href="/how-to-play/">how to play</a>.
  </p>
</InfoPageLayout>
